            <ArticleTitle>Delayed diagnosis of herpes zoster.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>57, 60, 63</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Herpes zoster may cause diagnostic confusion and mimic other diseases during the early stage before development of the characteristic rash. Although the disease is usually self-limited, oral acyclovir (Zovirax) shows promise in reducing the duration and severity of symptoms in uncomplicated cases.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
